The final content_shell link fails with:

    ioapi.c: undefined reference to `fopen64'
    ioapi.c: undefined reference to `fseeko64'
    ioapi.c: undefined reference to `ftello64'

minizip's ioapi.h aliases the LFS spellings back to the plain ones for
platforms whose libc lacks them, but its list is USE_FILE32API / __FreeBSD__ /
_MSC_VER. Haiku is none of those, so ioapi.c is compiled against glibc-style
names that Haiku's libroot does not have.

Haiku's plain fopen/fseeko/ftello are already 64-bit capable and this build
passes _FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64 globally, so aliasing is correct here for exactly
the reason it is correct on FreeBSD.

--- a/chromium/third_party/zlib/contrib/minizip/ioapi.h
+++ b/chromium/third_party/zlib/contrib/minizip/ioapi.h
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@
 #define ftello64 ftell
 #define fseeko64 fseek
 #else
-#ifdef __FreeBSD__
+#if defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__HAIKU__)
 #define fopen64 fopen
 #define ftello64 ftello
 #define fseeko64 fseeko
